  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i+j)^{2}=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i+j)^{2} & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(i+j)^{2}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}((1+j)^{2}+(2+j)^{2}+(3+j)^{2}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}((1+j)^{2}+(2+j)^{2}+(3+j)^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}((1+j)^{2}+(2+j)^{2}+(3+j)^{2}) & =((1+1)^{2}+(2+1)^{2}+(3+1)^{2})+((1+2)^{2}+(2+2)^{2}+(3+2)^{2}) \\\\  & =(4+9+16)+(9+16+25) \\\\  & =79\\end{aligned}\n$$",
